      "claim_excerpt": "## Summary\n\nUnder the same gate `p \u2265 max(64, 4K + 2C)` and `16 g ceil(log2 p) \u2264 p`,\n\n```text\n2 g (9 p^2 + p^6 exp(-p^2))^{g-1} p^6 exp(K p - p^2) < 2^{-C p}\n```\n\nfor integers `p \u2265 2`, `g \u2265 1`, `K \u2265 0` and `C \u2265 0`. The approximant exponent without this factor is at most `-C p - 4`. The factor 2 is one bit, so the remaining slack is 3 and the exponent above is at most `-C p - 3`.\n\nThe base stays strictly below `16 p^2` because `p^6 exp(-p^2) < 1/2` for `p \u2265 64` and `9 p^2 + 1 < 16 p^2`. This does not identify HALO's `2g` rectangles with the tensor difference. The section ceiling and the section error stay hypotheses. At `g = p^2` the monomial is still greater than 1. No new \u03ba. The selected record remains `23/10000`.\n\nThis answers the open question of #4497. It does not replay #4497. #4487 spends the same bit on the coefficient 10. One tensor axis is left open.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `python3.12 -B scripts/research_package.py --package research/gaussian-tensor-nine-faces`\n- [x] Prints `PASS_GAUSSIAN_TENSOR_NINE_FACES` and `outcome=completed`\n- [ ] Maintainer replay was not run\n\nBase `2a13eb1827784206202db90e5dc8327cf8a250db`, priority revision 7. Upstream fetched at 2026-10-22T02:42:08Z was still that commit, and the pre-submit fetch was unchanged.\n\nPrepared by James Reed with substantial Cursor Grok 4.7 assistance.\n",
